Location: app/assets/stylesheets/common/foundation/mixins.scss:117 (RIGHT)

Add the legacy Firefox alignment fallback to the flexbox mixin

Trigger: Use the new mixin in a Firefox version that supports the prefixed `-moz-box`/`-moz-inline-box` display syntax but does not support unprefixed `align-items`.

Impact: The prefixed flex container renders, but cross-axis centering or baseline alignment is ignored, leaving header and small-action contents vertically misaligned.

Evidence: @mixin align-items($alignment) {
    -webkit-box-align: $alignment;
    -webkit-align-items: $alignment;
    -ms-flex-align: $alignment;  
    -ms-align-items: $alignment;
    align-items:$alignment;
}

Suggested fix: Emit `-moz-box-align: $alignment` alongside the existing legacy display fallback, or remove the obsolete Mozilla display fallback and explicitly limit the supported browser range.

